#NEXUS

[ wilson2002a_fig13: Panel A, read by eye at 1.2-2x. Fourteen clade names at node circles are kept as internal labels (SAUROPODA, EUSAUROPODA, NEOSAUROPODA, DIPLODOCOIDEA, REBBACHISAURIDAE, DICRAEOSAURIDAE, DIPLODOCIDAE, MACRONARIA, TITANOSAURIFORMES, SOMPHOSPONDYLI, TITANOSAURIA, SALTASAURIDAE, OPISTHOCOELICAUDIINAE, SALTASAURINAE). Where a tip's line runs through a node circle and on down as the stem (Nigersaurus, Amargasaurus, Opisthocoelicaudia, Saltasaurus), the tip is a child of that node. Nemegtosaurus joins Rapetosaurus by a short solid bracket; the two dashed arrows (from that bracket and from the Opisthocoelicaudiinae circle to the 'T.' colberti junction) mark alternative placements and are not part of the gold tree. One three-way node: REBBACHISAURIDAE (Nigersaurus, Rebbachisaurus, Rayososaurus). 27 tips, 1 polytomies (3 children); 14 printed clade names kept as internal node labels. Sample 6 case (census 2 extended to draw 120, seed 20261231). Topology transcribed from the figure image and checked node by node; topology only. ]

